.TH LZR 1 "2026-11-28" "lzr 0.15.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lzr, unlzr, lzrcat \- compress or decompress .lzr files (LZR 1.0)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lzr
.RI [ OPTION ]... " " [ FILE ]...
.br
.B unlzr
is
.BR "lzr \-d" ;
.B lzrcat
is
.BR "lzr \-dc" .
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lzr
compresses each
.I FILE
to
.IR FILE .lzr
and removes the original, or with
.B \-d
restores it, keeping permissions and timestamps, in the manner of
.BR xz (1).
With no
.IR FILE ,
or when
.I FILE
is
.BR \- ,
it reads standard input and writes standard output, so it can be used as
.B tar \-I lzr
or in a pipe. Concatenated .lzr frames decompress to the concatenation of
their contents. Every frame carries a checksum (XXH64) of its content that is
verified on decompression.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-compress
Compress (the default).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decompress ", " \-\-uncompress
Decompress.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Decompress and verify without writing anything.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Print frames, segments, compressed and uncompressed sizes of .lzr files
(reads block headers only).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-stdout ", " \-\-to\-stdout
Write to standard output and keep input files.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep input files.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite existing output files, write compressed data to a terminal,
compress files that already have the suffix or have several hard links.
.TP
.BR \-0 " ... " \-11
Compression level (default 6). Levels 0\-10 decode at zstd\-class speed;
level 11 gives the best ratio (xz \-9 class).
.TP
.BR \-\-fast [ =\fIN\fR ]
Level \-\fIN\fR, \fIN\fR = 1..3 (default 1): fastest compression.
.TP
.BI \-\-level= N
Level \-3..11.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-threads=\fIN\fR
Worker threads (default 1; 0 = one per CPU, at most 16). Compressed output
does not depend on
.I N
(at levels \-3..6, it is the same for any
.I N
> 1). Decompression with
.I N
> 1 decodes segments and blocks in parallel when the input is a regular file
whose frames record their size.
.TP
.BI \-\-segment= SIZE
Start a new independent segment every
.I SIZE
bytes (suffixes K, M, G; at least 1MiB; 0 = off) so that the output can be
decompressed in parallel. Default: 48MiB at levels 9\-11, off otherwise.
.TP
.BI \-\-window\-log= N
Match window of 2^\fIN\fR bytes, \fIN\fR = 18..26 (default by level; levels
9\-11 use at least 2^20).
.TP
.B \-\-x86
Filter x86/x86\-64 CALL instructions first (better ratio on executables).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-window\-log= N
Refuse frames whose window is above 2^\fIN\fR bytes (18..31, default 27);
this bounds decoder memory.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-suffix=\fI.SUF\fR
Suffix of compressed files (default .lzr).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress warnings.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report sizes, ratio and speed for each file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 when only warnings occurred (for example a file
skipped or trailing garbage after the last frame).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
lzr \-9 \-T4 big.tar            # big.tar.lzr
lzr \-dc big.tar.lzr | tar xf \-
tar \-I 'lzr \-11 \-T0' \-cf src.tar.lzr src/
tar \-I lzr \-xf src.tar.lzr
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xz (1),
.BR zstd (1),
.BR tar (1).
The format is specified in docs/FORMAT.md of the lzrans sources.
